<template>
    <heading>Operations</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>operations</li>
        <li>generator</li>
        <li>coroutine</li>
        <li>command handler</li>
        <li>initialization</li>
        <li>to_handler</li>
        <li>modal dialog</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code>operations</code> holds the application's multi-step command handlers. Each handler is a generator object, created and primed by <code>to_handler</code>. The generator receives <code>self</code>, a function that returns its own object; calling <code>self()</code> after construction avoids accessing the object before it exists.</p>
        <p>Each operation can produce one of three outcomes when <code>controller</code> resumes it with <code>handler.next(command)</code>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><code>yield self()</code>: remain the current handler. The controller stops dispatching this command; the next command resumes the same operation.</li>
            <li><code>yield child</code>, where <code>child</code> is another primed generator object: call a child operation. The controller pushes <code>child</code> onto <code>handlerStack</code> and immediately dispatches the same command to it.</li>
            <li><code>return</code>, or reach the end of the generator: finish the operation. The generator result has <code>done === true</code>, so the controller pops it and resumes the parent with the same command. Any returned value is ignored. If no parent remains, dispatch ends.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>A <code>ModalDialog</code> command carries a <code>dialogName</code> key identifying the dialog-specific operation. The base handler switches on that key and yields the selected primed operation. The controller then sends the same initial command to the child.</p>
        <p><code>SelectCreateProject</code> is the operation for the startup project dialog. It receives the initial command and calls <code>showModalDialog</code> with the dialog template's DOM id. The helper finds that child template inside <code>LP5-Dialog-Templates</code> and uses <code>util.mountTemplate</code> to clone and append it while compiling its script with the element-ID map. The script returns the mounted dialog. The helper inserts a clone of the first child shared modal style before the dialog's own style, then calls <code>showModal()</code>. It returns immediately; the operation remains the active handler and can receive later commands while the dialog is open.</p>
        <p>The Select button dispatches <code>SelectProject</code>. The <code>SelectCreateProject</code> operation yields the new <code>SelectProject</code> handler for that command. The handler invokes <code>showDirectoryPicker()</code> synchronously while the button's user activation is still active, then returns; cancellation is ignored and other picker errors are logged. Handling the selected directory is a later step. The Create button still dispatches <code>Create</code>, which refers to the not-yet-written <code>CreateProjectOperation</code> bundle.</p>
        <p><code>operations</code> installs the primed base handler with <code>controller.init(handler)</code> before any commands are dispatched.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>JavaScript units</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
let operations = (() => {
    function to_handler(generator) {
        const handler = generator(() => handler);
        handler.next();
        return handler;
    }

    function showModalDialog(dialogName) {
        const templates = document.getElementById("LP5-Dialog-Templates");
        if (!(templates instanceof HTMLTemplateElement))
            throw new Error("Missing LP5-Dialog-Templates template");

        const template = templates.content.querySelector(`#${dialogName}`);
        if (!(template instanceof HTMLTemplateElement))
            throw new Error(`Missing dialog template: ${dialogName}`);

        const sharedStyle = templates.content.firstElementChild;
        if (!(sharedStyle instanceof HTMLStyleElement))
            throw new Error("Missing shared dialog styles");

        const dialog = util.mountTemplate(template, document.body);
        if (!(dialog instanceof HTMLDialogElement))
            throw new Error(`Dialog template script did not return a dialog: ${dialogName}`);

        const dialogStyle = dialog.previousElementSibling;
        if (!(dialogStyle instanceof HTMLStyleElement))
            throw new Error(`Dialog template has no dialog styles: ${dialogName}`);

        dialogStyle.before(sharedStyle.cloneNode(true));
        dialog.showModal();
    }

    function* SelectProject(self) {
        yield self();
        window.showDirectoryPicker().catch(error => {
            if (error.name !== "AbortError")
                console.error(error);
        });
    }

    function* SelectCreateProject(self) {
        let command = yield self();
        showModalDialog("SelectCreateProject");
        while (true) {
            command = yield self();
            switch (command.name) {
            case "SelectProject":
                yield to_handler(SelectProject);
                break;
            case "Create":
                yield ]]><lp5- ref="CreateProjectOperation"/><![CDATA[;
                break;
            }
        }
    }

    function* baseOperationsHandler(self) {
        while (true) {
            let command = yield self();
            if (command.name === "ModalDialog") {
                switch (command.dialogName) {
                case "SelectCreateProject":
                    yield to_handler(SelectCreateProject);
                    break;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    const handler = to_handler(baseOperationsHandler);
    controller.init(handler);

    return {};
})();
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
